## Standard Cell Library and PVT Characterization

A standard cell library contains pre-designed and pre-characterized digital logic cells such as **AND, OR, NAND, NOR gates, multiplexers, and flip-flops** that are used during logic synthesis.

Each cell is characterized under specific **Process, Voltage, and Temperature (PVT)** conditions to accurately represent its timing, power, and area characteristics.

For example, the library **`sky130_fd_sc_hd__tt_025C_1v80.lib`** represents the SKY130 High-Density standard cell library characterized for the **Typical-Typical (TT)** process corner, an operating temperature of **25°C**, and a supply voltage of **1.80 V**.

These parameters help synthesis and timing analysis tools estimate circuit performance under defined operating conditions, ensuring reliable hardware implementation despite manufacturing variations and environmental changes.
